### Request collection (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP Client)
### Start the API first: python manage.py runserver (from backend/, with DJANGO_DEBUG=1).
### Requests that change data need the CSRF token from request 1, kept in {{csrf}}.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

### 0. Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Get the CSRF token (also sets the csrftoken cookie)
# @name csrfToken
GET {{base}}/auth/csrf

@csrf = {{csrfToken.response.body.csrf}}

### 2. Typeahead
GET {{base}}/geocode/search?q=Memphis&limit=5

### 3. Name a point (Kearney, Nebraska)
GET {{base}}/geocode/reverse?lat=40.7&lon=-99.08

### 4. Plan the example trip: Dallas, Memphis, Denver, 24 hours already used
POST {{base}}/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current": { "label": "Dallas, Texas, United States", "lat": 32.7767, "lon": -96.797 },
  "pickup": { "label": "Memphis, Tennessee, United States", "lat": 35.1495, "lon": -90.049 },
  "dropoff": { "label": "Denver, Colorado, United States", "lat": 39.7392, "lon": -104.9903 },
  "cycle_used_hours": 24,
  "departure": "2026-10-07T06:00",
  "timezone": "America/Chicago",
  "header": { "driver_name": "Sam Rivera", "carrier_name": "Rivera Freight", "truck_number": "101" }
}

### 5. Validation error: cycle hours over 70 -> 400 validation_error with fields
POST {{base}}/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current": { "label": "Dallas, TX", "lat": 32.7767, "lon": -96.797 },
  "pickup": { "label": "Memphis, TN", "lat": 35.1495, "lon": -90.049 },
  "dropoff": { "label": "Denver, CO", "lat": 39.7392, "lon": -104.9903 },
  "cycle_used_hours": 95,
  "departure": "2026-10-07T06:00",
  "timezone": "America/Chicago"
}

### 6. A cycle that runs out: 60 hours used on a long trip -> plan includes a 34-hour restart
POST {{base}}/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current": { "label": "Los Angeles, California, United States", "lat": 34.0522, "lon": -118.2437 },
  "pickup": { "label": "Phoenix, Arizona, United States", "lat": 33.4484, "lon": -112.074 },
  "dropoff": { "label": "New York, New York, United States", "lat": 40.7128, "lon": -74.006 },
  "cycle_used_hours": 60,
  "departure": "2026-10-07T06:00",
  "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles"
}

### 7. Create an account (signs you in; the session cookie is kept by the client)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}

{ "email": "driver@example.com", "password": "a-long-passphrase-123", "name": "Sam" }

### 8. Sign in
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}

{ "email": "driver@example.com", "password": "a-long-passphrase-123" }

### 9. Who am I
GET {{base}}/auth/me

### 10. Save a trip (the server plans it again from `request`)
# @name saved
POST {{base}}/trips
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}

{
  "title": "Dallas to Denver via Memphis",
  "request": {
    "current": { "label": "Dallas, Texas, United States", "lat": 32.7767, "lon": -96.797 },
    "pickup": { "label": "Memphis, Tennessee, United States", "lat": 35.1495, "lon": -90.049 },
    "dropoff": { "label": "Denver, Colorado, United States", "lat": 39.7392, "lon": -104.9903 },
    "cycle_used_hours": 24,
    "departure": "2026-10-07T06:00",
    "timezone": "America/Chicago"
  }
}

@tripId = {{saved.response.body.id}}

### 11. List my trips
GET {{base}}/trips?limit=20&offset=0

### 12. Open one trip
GET {{base}}/trips/{{tripId}}

### 13. Rename it
PATCH {{base}}/trips/{{tripId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}

{ "title": "Renamed trip" }

### 14. Delete it
DELETE {{base}}/trips/{{tripId}}
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}

### 15. Someone else's trip, or one that doesn't exist -> 404
GET {{base}}/trips/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### 16. Sign out
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
X-CSRFToken: {{csrf}}
